# mm.touch.cst328

The Hynitron CST328 capacitive touch controller, over portable mm.mcu I2C and
GPIO. It contains no vendor header and no board pin number: a board's provider
supplies the wiring and this module drives the protocol.

The register map is sixteen-bit and big-endian, which is why every access here
is an mm.mcu i2c_write_read rather than a write followed by a read: the
controller's address pointer must not be exposed to another master between the
two halves.

Modelled on Waveshare's reference driver for the RP2350-Touch-LCD-2.8. Two
things in that driver are deliberately not reproduced. Its interrupt handler is
absent, because mm.touch is polled and mm.mcu has no callback registration. Its
rotation transform is absent, because mm.touch reports the panel's own
coordinates and rotation belongs to whoever knows how the panel is mounted.
